<title>USA: Tower won't pay Q4 dividend to save cash.</title>
<headline>Tower won't pay Q4 dividend to save cash.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tower Air said on Tuesday it would not pay a dividend on its stock in the fourth quarter, in order to conserve cash.</p>
<p>The company also said the U.S. District Court of Appeals affirmed a District Court order approving the settlement of class action suits arising out of the company's 1993 initial stock offering.</p>
<p>&quot;The Court of Appeals' affirmance confirms the settlement and concludes all litigation related to the company's stock offering,&quot; said Morris Nachtomi, president, chief executive officer and chairman.</p>
</text>
